From: jahshaka <jahshaka@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clusterlod: the prune's clause (2) is decided by the verify hook (clodMesh::verify_group's prune_budget); the hook sees the group's locks

ATOM-7, 2026-10-21. Patch 0004's prune has two clauses: (1) whole unlocked
components smallest first up to simplify_threshold x the input at any price (the
level is accepted, never terminal while an unlocked piece exists), and (2) on
toward the halving target only within a budget. 0004 priced clause (2) inside the
library: simplify_prune_budget x max(*error, the smallest piece) — and *error is
the attribute quadric, 8-100x the measured deviation above depth 0 (every merged
group crosses UV seams), so every island was "within budget" and the floor
admitted every island equal to the smallest (Bistro: nine 58 cm shutters pruned
from a facade whose level deviated 8.6 cm). The deformation exists in one place,
the caller's verify, so clause (2) is decided there:

- clodMesh::verify_group gains two parameters: `const unsigned char* locks` (the
  group's lock array as the result was simplified: the level's boundary, terminal
  and input locks plus the hook's own CLOD_LOCK_VERIFY ones), and
  `float* prune_budget` (out; -1 before the call). A NULL answer with a budget >= 0
  asks for clause (2) under that ABSOLUTE budget.
- simplify() keeps the collapses' result (before the prune) and its error
  (`Collapsed`); the first prune of every result is clause (1) alone.
- verifyGroup: after a NULL answer with a budget, the group is RE-PRUNED from the
  kept collapses' result (`repruneFrom`: no second simplification; clause (1) as
  before, then clause (2) under the budget) and the re-pruned result is verified
  again — it counts as an attempt (CLOD_VERIFY_MAX_RETRIES bounds both); at most
  one re-prune per simplified result, and one that removes nothing more is final
  (the accepted result stands). A lock answer re-simplifies as before (clause (1)
  only), then the budget cycle again.
- clodConfig::simplify_prune_budget is DELETED (the default config never sets a
  budget: without a hook clause (2) never runs).
- clodGroup::simplify_flags gains CLOD_SIMPLIFY_REPRUNED (clause (2) removed at
  least one more piece).
- The edge-limit adjustment moves into a helper (limitErrorByEdges), called after
  either prune.
- THE BEST ATTEMPT WINS (round 2, the lead's rule after the stage-1 stop): the
  hook answers a bound for every result (`result_bound`), and the group keeps,
  among its verified attempts, the one with the LOWEST bound (ties: the smaller
  result, then the earlier attempt) — never simply the last: a retry under added
  locks could miss the collapses it needed and have clause (1) pay a whole wall
  at any price (Bistro: a 16.9 m island at d1 where attempt 0 deviated 4.94 m;
  the runtime sphere emptied at d1). A retry stuck above simplify_threshold is
  not verified and an earlier attempt is kept (terminal only when the first
  result was stuck, as before). After the last attempt the hook is called once
  more with attempt = -1 and `winner` = the kept attempt's number, with the kept
  result (its answer is ignored).

Applied at configure (irisgl/CMakeLists.txt) to a copy of the vendored header
in the build tree, after 0004; the vendored file itself is never edited.
